# Topical events

A topical-event page gathers information about a time-bounded subject. Its government crisis and policy context does not transfer directly to a household. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/topical-events/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

A household adaptation may gather a planned maintenance project, a seasonal setup or a documented upgrade. State the purpose, dates and current status. Separate a project’s background from live alerts and operational controls.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a concise introduction, current information and a curated list of related guides or records. An About page may explain scope and responsibility. Mark closed or archived projects and retain their history where it is useful. A decorative image is optional and needs a clear purpose.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not invent a campaign, crisis response or multi-agency authority. The template is reference guidance, not an event-management feature or automation scheduler. Examples use explicitly fictional projects and no household dates are inferred.

